# Cupp app environment — copy to .env and fill in real values (never commit .env)
# Ask Bryan for the two Supabase values over a private channel.
# These two are SAFE to ship in the app bundle: the anon key only permits what
# our Supabase row-level-security rules allow.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# NOTE: the Agnes/OpenAI key is NOT used by the app and must never appear here.
# It lives only in scripts/.env (server-side harness) and later in a Supabase
# Edge Function secret.

# 1 = real scan (upload + scan-bag Edge Function). Unset/0 = mock scan that
# always returns the SEY Huila fixture. Missing Supabase vars above ALSO force
# demo mode (mock scan + local fixture data, nothing hits the shared DB).
# After editing this file: restart Expo with `npx expo start -c` — EXPO_PUBLIC_
# vars are baked in at bundler start.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SCAN_LIVE=1
